STEP 5  the explicit worst configuration (realizable on the lattice)
  U_1(x)=(-1)^(x2+x3+x4),  U_mu(x)=(-1)^x1 (mu=2,3,4)  on an even torus.
  Then every (1,mu) plaque = -1 and every (mu,nu) plaque = +1, so a direction-1 link
  sits in 6 plaques all equal to the centre element -1: Hess S_W = -(3 beta/N) delta.
  The negative block is ISOTROPIC, so no metric shape can align anything with it;
  (star) at t=0 then needs  Ric_G > (6 beta/N) delta.
  SU(2) beta=2.5:  block = -3.7500 delta ;  needed lam_min(Ric_G) > 7.5000 ;  sup_G = 0.5000  ==> short by 15.00x  (Ric must be 15.00x larger)
  SU(3) beta=2.5:  block = -2.5000 delta ;  needed lam_min(Ric_G) > 5.0000 ;  sup_G = 0.7500  ==> short by 6.67x  (Ric must be 6.67x larger)

